    {
      "text": "Développer et réduire l'expression $(x+2)(x-3)$.",
      "options": [
        "$x^2 - x - 6$",
        "$x^2 + x - 6$",
        "$x^2 - 5x - 6$",
        "$x^2 + 5x - 6$"
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "$x^2 - x - 6$",
      "explanation": "En appliquant la distributivité : $(x+2)(x-3) = x(x-3) + 2(x-3) = x^2 - 3x + 2x - 6 = x^2 - x - 6$. Les autres options correspondent à des erreurs de signes ou de coefficients.",
      "points": 1,
      "figure": null
    },
    {
      "text": "Développer et réduire $2(x+3)^2 - 4(x+3)$.",
      "options": [
        "$2x^2 + 8x + 6$",
        "$2x^2 + 12x + 18$",
        "$2x^2 + 8x + 12$",
        "$2x^2 + 4x + 6$"
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "$2x^2 + 8x + 6$",
      "explanation": "On calcule $(x+3)^2 = x^2 + 6x + 9$, puis $2(x+3)^2 = 2x^2 + 12x + 18$. Ensuite $-4(x+3) = -4x - 12$. En additionnant : $2x^2 + 12x + 18 - 4x - 12 = 2x^2 + 8x + 6$.",
      "points": 1,
      "figure": null
    },
    {
      "text": "Simplifier $(3x-2)(2x+5) + (x-4)(x+1)$.",
      "options": [
        "$7x^2 + 8x - 14$",
        "$7x^2 + 14x - 14$",
        "$6x^2 + 8x - 14$",
        "$7x^2 + 8x - 6$"
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "$7x^2 + 8x - 14$",
      "explanation": "Premier produit : $(3x-2)(2x+5) = 6x^2 + 15x - 4x - 10 = 6x^2 + 11x - 10$. Second produit : $(x-4)(x+1) = x^2 + x - 4x - 4 = x^2 - 3x - 4$. Somme : $6x^2 + 11x - 10 + x^2 - 3x - 4 = 7x^2 + 8x - 14$.",
      "points": 1,
      "figure": null
    },
    {
      "text": "Développer et réduire $(2x-1)^2 - (x+2)(x-2)$.",
      "options": [
        "$3x^2 - 4x + 5$",
        "$3x^2 - 4x - 3$",
        "$5x^2 - 4x + 5$",
        "$3x^2 + 4x + 5$"
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "$3x^2 - 4x + 5$",
      "explanation": "On a $(2x-1)^2 = 4x^2 - 4x + 1$ et $(x+2)(x-2) = x^2 - 4$. La différence donne $4x^2 - 4x + 1 - (x^2 - 4) = 3x^2 - 4x + 5$.",
      "points": 1,
      "figure": null
    },
    {
      "text": "Réduire l'expression $A = (x+1)(x-1) + 2(x+2)^2 - 3x$.",
      "options": [
        "$3x^2 + 5x + 7$",
        "$3x^2 + 11x + 7$",
        "$3x^2 + 5x + 9$",
        "$2x^2 + 5x + 7$"
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "$3x^2 + 5x + 7$",
      "explanation": "On développe : $(x+1)(x-1) = x^2 - 1$. $2(x+2)^2 = 2(x^2 + 4x + 4) = 2x^2 + 8x + 8$. En ajoutant $-3x$ : $x^2 - 1 + 2x^2 + 8x + 8 - 3x = 3x^2 + 5x + 7$.",
